    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Horan Estates are delighted to present 187 Botanic Avenue, Drumcondra, Dublin 9 to the market — a charming and well-maintained three-bedroom mid-terrace Victorian-style red brick home situated on one of Dublin 9's most sought-after and tree-lined residential streets. Offering tremendous character throughout, this property presents an exciting opportunity for buyers looking to place their own stamp on a home in a truly superb location, with excellent scope for modernisation and improvement.\r\n\r\nThe ground floor accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hall leading to a bright living room with feature fireplace to the front, and a separate dining room with fireplace to the rear. The kitchen with fitted units and access to a rear patio courtyard is also on this level, along with a useful rear extension providing additional everyday space and a back door to the garden. Upstairs, three bedrooms are served by a landing, along with a separate WC. The rear garden provides additional outdoor space with a garden shed.\r\n\r\nBotanic Avenue is a well-regarded address within striking distance of some of Dublin's best schools and colleges. The area is also very well served by transport links with many bus services running up and down the Drumcondra Road, along with the train and the M1 and M50 which are all located just a few minutes' walk away offering swift access into and across the city and beyond. \r\n\r\nThe location is second to none with all amenities close by:\r\n\r\nWalking distance to Drumcondra Rail Station — fast rail access to Dublin City Centre and beyond \r\nShort walk to Griffith Park with beautiful walks along the River Tolka, playgrounds, and open green spaces \r\nShort walk to the National Botanic Gardens, Glasnevin\r\nWalking distance to DCU and St Patrick's College of Education \r\nNearby primary schools include Corpus Christi NS, Scoil Mobhi and Glasnevin NS; secondary schools include Dominican College, Scoil Caitriona, Holy Faith and Ard Scoil Rís \r\nHealthcare — Beaumont Hospital, mater and Bon Secours Hospital within easy reach \r\nShort walk to Drumcondra Village with shops, cafés, restaurants and bars\r\nCroke Park within walking distance\r\nConvenient to M50 and M1 motorways and Dublin Airport \r\nMultiple Dublin Bus routes providing frequent connections to Dublin City Centre\r\n\r\nThis is a rare opportunity to acquire a home of genuine character and potential on one of Drumcondra's finest streets. \r\n\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: Please note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, furniture, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate, and photographs are provided for guidance only. Furniture shown is for representation purposes only; please consult the estate agent to confirm what will remain in the property."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Ground Floor\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall – 11.23 m² (2.17 × 6.61) | Carpet flooring, staircase to first floor\r\n\r\nLiving Room – 12.96 m² (3.52 × 3.68) | Feature fireplace, carpet flooring, window to front\r\n\r\nDining Room – 10.09 m² (2.71 × 3.72) | Feature fireplace, window to rear\r\n\r\nKitchen – 8.03 m² (2.45 × 3.47) | Fitted floor and wall units, tiled flooring, access to rear\r\n\r\nRear Hall – 2.14 m² (2.45 × 0.88) | Access to rear courtyard and garden\r\n\r\nBathroom (Ground Floor) – 4.74 m² (2.45 × 1.94) | Fully tiled shower room, WC, wash hand basin\r\n\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\n\r\nLanding – 8.76 m² (1.80 × 4.87) | Carpet flooring, access to all rooms\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 – 12.00 m² (3.12 × 3.85) | Double bedroom, built-in wardrobes, carpet flooring, window to rear\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 – 7.91 m² (2.19 × 3.61) | Double bedroom, carpet flooring, window to front\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 – 4.68 m² (1.80 × 2.60) | Single bedroom, carpet flooring\r\n\r\nBathroom (First Floor) – 1.56 m² (0.80 × 1.96) | WC, wash hand basin\r\n\r\n\r\nTotal Floor Area: approximately 92 m²"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Charming three-bedroom Victorian-style red brick mid-terrace on one of Drumcondra's most sought-after streets\r\nTwo reception rooms, both with feature fireplaces\r\nRear extension providing additional living space\r\nPrivate rear courtyard and garden with shed\r\nModern shower room on ground floor\r\nExcellent scope for modernisation and personalisation throughout\r\nWalking distance to Drumcondra Rail Station and multiple bus routes\r\nWithin walking distance of Drumcondra Village, shops, cafés and restaurants\r\nClose to excellent primary and secondary schools including Dominican College and Corpus Christi NS\r\nMinutes from Griffith Park, the National Botanic Gardens and Croke Park"
